<h2 id="trigger-cdcm" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Trigger `cdcm`</h2>

When the prompt contains **`cdcm`** as a **whole-word** token, the user wants **comment and docstring enhancement** following **section 1** above.

- **Scope:** If the user names **specific modules, files, directories, or classes**, limit edits to those targets (and their closely related symbols). If they **do not** name any scope, interpret **`cdcm`** as: apply **section 1** across **relevant source** in the **current project**—prioritize packages and entrypoints the project actually uses; avoid drive-by rewrites of vendored or generated trees unless the user includes them.
- **Goal:** Satisfy [section 2](#cdcm-per-symbol) on scoped files, plus file headers and **non-obvious** inline notes—**intent**, **invariants**, **gotchas**—not noise.

**Note:** **`alwaysApply: true`** keeps these norms in context; adding **`cdcm`** means **perform** a comment/doc pass **now** per sections 1–3 (scoped as above).

